>
> The game knows when "Elbereth" is *there*. Determining whether *you*
> engraved it is a different question.

   Well, the only way that a you-engraved "Elbereth" can get on the floor
is via an (E)ngrave action, right?  So all the game has to do is check
the floor before and after every (E)ngrave, and if there is an "Elbereth"
there after the action that wasn't there before, you must have engraved
it.

   I am assuming that the idea of "Elberethless" is also meant to include
"Elberet" "hless", "Elbe" "rethless", and so on. ;)  The method I
described would prevent the Elberethless conduct player from engraving
"Elbereth" over multiple turns, as well as in a single turn. If that's
not what you were thinking of, or if you've got some other subtle
difference in mind, please say it. :)

   Tracking this conduct would require another conduct flag in the save
file, so it might break save-file compatibility (unless there are extra
unused conduct flags already, which seems highly likely to me;
IHTSIFOMBITLTL). But it shouldn't be hard to implement.

